   "lines": [
    [
     "c14_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "How does turning *a wheel* turn the wheels?",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "rack"
      }
     },
     "How does turning a round wheel in your hands point the tyres left and right?"
    ],
    [
     "c14_2",
     {
      "label": "pinion",
      "head": "A small gear: the *pinion*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "rack"
      }
     },
     "At the bottom of the steering column is a small gear, called the pinion."
    ],
    [
     "c14_3",
     {
      "label": "rack",
      "head": "It moves a *rack* sideways",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "rack"
      }
     },
     "It meshes with a toothed bar, the rack. Turning the pinion slides the rack left or right."
    ],
    [
     "c14_4",
     {
      "label": "tie rods",
      "head": "*Tie rods* push the wheels",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "rack"
      }
     },
     "Tie rods on each end of the rack push and pull the front wheels, so they point where you want."
    ],
    [
     "c14_5",
     {
      "label": "assist",
      "head": "Power steering *helps* you",
      "pose": "cheer",
      "face": "happy",
      "prop": {
       "type": "rack",
       "assist": true,
       "label": "ELECTRIC POWER STEERING"
      }
     },
     "Without help, steering a parked car is hard work. Older cars use a hydraulic pump. Most new cars use an electric motor."
    ],
    [
     "c14_6",
     {
      "label": "alignment",
      "head": "Alignment keeps it *straight*",
      "pose": "think",
